oying the "dark side" phrase poetically, too**—nothing about the science demands you strip the phrase from your vocabulary or stop finding it evocative. Pink Floyd didn't do worse art by using an inaccurate phrase. The mysterious feeling doesn't have to be tied to strict literal accuracy to still be worth enjoying.
